  "instruction": "Using only the FTC section `What To Do About Spam Text Messages` in Edge Immersive Reader, draft an email to `family@example.org` with subject `Spam text safety`. Use the FTC's exact wording to state what to do about links in an unexpected text asking for personal or financial information and how to contact a company if the message may be real. Do not paraphrase or add outside information. Save the draft and leave Immersive Reader open.",
  "source": "https://consumer.ftc.gov/articles/how-recognize-and-report-spam-text-messages",
  "gt_steps": [
    "Open the FTC guidance in Microsoft Edge.",
    "Press `F9` to enter Immersive Reader.",
    "Read the section `What To Do About Spam Text Messages`.",
    "Open Thunderbird and create a new email draft.",
    "Set the recipient to `family@example.org`.",
    "Set the subject to `Spam text safety`.",
    "Enter the following message body: don't click on any links\ncontact the company using a phone number or website you know is real\nNot the information in the text message",
    "Save the draft without sending it."
  ],
